From 1e533f8e7ad107390c944105a3af8dbd4b165989 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IeumOffice <dev@ieumoffice.local>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:23:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(layout): exclude owner column from body-wide Para float
 reservation

In a multi-column layout, a body-wide TopAndBottom floating table or shape
with VertRelTo::Para belongs to its anchor column and is laid out in flow
at the anchor paragraph. Previously calculate_body_wide_shape_reserved
applied its reserved bottom to every column including the owner column,
pre-pushing the owner column y_offset before laying out the anchor
paragraph so the table shifted down by its own height and overlapped both
following paragraphs in column 0 and column 1.

Track the owner column index for VertRelTo::Para reservations and filter
it out when laying out that column, compute body-wide table geometry with
absolute_table_vertical_geometry so outer top/bottom margins are included,
and include column-0 first-paragraph VertRelTo::Para head objects in
page_head_bottom so the column separator starts below the head table.
